  "player_text": "I step away from the guard and go to the notice board he indicated. I read the postings for the taxes, the curfew, and anything that says what a traveler needs in order to pass.",
  "visible_motivation": "The guard refused a number and told me the board lists the current taxes, curfew, and passage expectations.",
  "intended_meaning": "Read the notice board for taxes, curfew, and passage requirements.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "You step closer to the notice board pressed against the rain-darkened stone of the gate district. The board holds several notices: new tax rates affecting travelers linger at the top, imposed recently by the city magistrate. Below that, curfew hours are clearly posted, forbidding movement past the gates after dusk without explicit guard permission. A separate pinned warning mentions a patrol gone missing on the northwest route beyond the crates, cautioning travelers to report any unusual sights. There is no explicit mention here of any specific papers required for entry, but fees and permits are suggested to be in constant flux, as the gate guard showed uncertainty earlier. It appears the most reliable information remains with the gate officials who enforce these rules day by day.",
  "generation_attempt_2": "The notice board before you is densely packed with papers under a thin layer of grime from the rain. You make out several postings: a list of new taxes imposed recently, a curfew ordinance restricting movement after dark, and a cautionary note about a patrol reported missing to the northwest. While there is no direct statement detailing traveler-specific papers or fees here, the implication of frequent changes and the posted warnings suggest that travelers might face variable requirements. Nearby guards keep a watchful eye on the board and the crowd, but do not intervene as you read.",
